From: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] No update check at launch; never offer the x86_64 AppImage

Class:   LOCAL WORKAROUND (distribution packaging: pacman owns updates).
Applies: open-chess v1.3.0 (patch -p1 from the repository root).
Why:     with checkUpdatesOnLaunch defaulting to true, every start asks
         api.github.com for the latest release and, when it is newer, offers
         to download "this OS's installer": on Linux the release's .AppImage,
         which is x86_64. Here the launch-time check defaults to off (a
         setting the user can still turn on), and on Linux the Download button
         goes to the release page rather than to a binary for another
         architecture. Settings > Check for updates still works.
---
--- a/lib/src/state/settings.dart
+++ b/lib/src/state/settings.dart
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
     this.textScale = 1.0,
     this.localeCode,
     this.playerProfile = const PlayerProfile(),
-    this.checkUpdatesOnLaunch = true,
+    this.checkUpdatesOnLaunch = false,
   });
 
   BoardThemeOption get theme {
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@
     // Older settings files simply omit profile data. Also accept the
     // temporary flat shape so no local identity is lost during migration.
     playerProfile: _profileFromJson(j),
-    checkUpdatesOnLaunch: j['checkUpdatesOnLaunch'] as bool? ?? true,
+    checkUpdatesOnLaunch: j['checkUpdatesOnLaunch'] as bool? ?? false,
   );
 
   static PlayerProfile _profileFromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) {
--- a/lib/src/state/update_service.dart
+++ b/lib/src/state/update_service.dart
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@
   final suffix = switch (os) {
     'android' => '.apk',
     'windows' => '.exe',
-    'linux' => '.appimage',
+    // Distribution package: the upstream AppImage is x86_64, and pacman owns
+    // updates here, so Download goes to the release page instead.
+    'linux' => null,
     _ => null,
   };
   if (suffix == null) return null;
